roundcube (1.4.6+dfsg.1-3) unstable; urgency=low

  The roundcube-plugins package no longer ships

      /usr/share/roundcube/plugins/enigma/openpgp.min.js

  due to DFSG violation.  Roundcube was only using this file for OpenPGP key
  generation as part of the enigma plugin; other key operations, including
  encryption, decryption, signature verification, keyserver handling etc. all
  still work.  Roundcube users can also create key pairs locally and import
  them into Roundcube at /?_task=settings&_action=plugin.enigmakeys.

  Site administrators wanting to preserve key generation ability in enigma
  need to manually copy

      https://raw.githubusercontent.com/openpgpjs/openpgpjs/v4.4.6/dist/openpgp.min.js

  (or a later version) to /usr/share/roundcube/plugins/enigma/openpgp.min.js .
  Note that while OpenPGP.js isn't in Debian yet, there is an open Request For
  Packaging (#787774).

  To use OpenPGP with Roundcube, an alternative/complement to the enigma
  plugin is Mailvelope, a browser extension providing support for client-side
  signing/decryption which works natively with Roundcube core and doesn't
  require copying private key material to the server.  See the following blog
  post for details:

      https://kolabian.wordpress.com/2015/10/10/mailvelope-integration-pgp-encryption/

 -- Guilhem Moulin <guilhem@debian.org>  Sat, 04 Jul 2020 01:07:51 +0200
